What's wrong, sir?

279
00:12:46,900 --> 00:12:50,340
Have either of you heard tell of a place called Arendam Village?

280
00:12:50,340 --> 00:12:52,260
It's in the Forsaken Realm

281
00:12:52,260 --> 00:12:54,340
I happened upon it while I was out wandering

282
00:12:54,340 --> 00:12:58,180
I mean investigating different areas of the Clover Kingdom

283
00:12:58,180 --> 00:13:03,700
According to several reports, Arendam Village has begun to suffer from a bandit problem recently

284
00:13:03,700 --> 00:13:06,020
Then we should send a team there to deal with them

285
00:13:06,020 --> 00:13:08,260
No, that won't be enough to solve this

286
00:13:08,820 --> 00:13:12,500
I'm not sure why, but I have a feeling that something unfavorable is going on

287
00:13:13,060 --> 00:13:14,420
The only question is what?

288
00:13:15,380 --> 00:13:16,580
Something unfavorable?

289
00:13:17,540 --> 00:13:18,740
Sounds ominous

290
00:13:18,740 --> 00:13:20,340
That's where you two come in

291
00:13:20,340 --> 00:13:23,060
You'll disguise yourselves and mingle with the villagers

292
00:13:23,060 --> 00:13:26,260
Perhaps that way you'll learn something useful about the bandits

293
00:13:26,260 --> 00:13:28,340
It's an undercover investigation

294
00:13:28,980 --> 00:13:30,580
Sounds like he's thought this through

295
00:13:31,780 --> 00:13:33,380
Are these really our disguises?

296
00:13:34,260 --> 00:13:38,340
Listen, I hate to criticize, but this only makes us look more suspicious

297
00:13:39,300 --> 00:13:41,380
These outfits are our only hope

298
00:13:41,380 --> 00:13:43,540
We don't know how to conduct ourselves like commoners

299
00:13:43,540 --> 00:13:45,940
So our best strategy is to hide our appearance altogether

300
00:13:46,740 --> 00:13:49,540
Some nobles do forsake their lives of luxury

301
00:13:49,540 --> 00:13:52,260
Perhaps people will assume that's the case with us

302
00:13:52,260 --> 00:13:54,180
Right, that makes sense

303
00:13:54,180 --> 00:13:57,300
Anyway, where should we begin gathering intel?

304
00:13:57,300 --> 00:13:59,220
The village square is as good a place as any

305
00:14:00,180 --> 00:14:02,660
Perfectly sound, and lest we forget

306
00:14:02,660 --> 00:14:05,460
The Wizard King said we're supposed to act casual

307
00:14:05,460 --> 00:14:07,060
So let's do our best to blend in

308
00:14:09,300 --> 00:14:11,460
Blending in isn't their strong suit

309
00:14:12,100 --> 00:14:14,820
Maybe if they could relax we'd be able to pull it off

310
00:14:14,820 --> 00:14:16,900
But I mustn't overstep my station

311
00:14:24,340 --> 00:14:25,700
What happened here?

312
00:14:26,980 --> 00:14:29,460
We knew there were areas that hadn't been restored yet

313
00:14:29,460 --> 00:14:31,620
But this is true devastation

314
00:14:31,620 --> 00:14:32,740
It's unspeakable

315
00:14:32,740 --> 00:14:35,620
We'll have time to address this matter eventually

316
00:14:35,620 --> 00:14:38,180
We need to focus on the mission at hand

317
00:14:38,180 --> 00:14:39,540
I'll go this way

318
00:14:39,540 --> 00:14:41,700
I'll try here

319
00:14:41,700 --> 00:14:45,060
Pardon me

320
00:14:45,060 --> 00:14:48,580
Hello there, I don't believe we've met before

321
00:14:48,580 --> 00:14:50,980
I'm Leon, I'm a traveling mage

322
00:14:50,980 --> 00:14:52,900
Yes, and the same goes for me

323
00:14:52,900 --> 00:14:54,180
My name's Mark

324
00:14:54,180 --> 00:14:56,180
Traveling mages, eh?

325
00:14:56,820 --> 00:14:59,380
We heard about the bandits that target this place

326
00:14:59,380 --> 00:15:01,300
And we'd like you to tell us everything you know

327
00:15:01,300 --> 00:15:03,060
So that we can protect ourselves

328
00:15:03,060 --> 00:15:04,900
I don't know Jack

329
00:15:04,900 --> 00:15:06,740
Why don't you go bother somebody else?

330
00:15:06,740 --> 00:15:09,140
I've never seen guys like those before

331
00:15:09,140 --> 00:15:12,020
They're wary of us because of these so-called disguises

332
00:15:12,980 --> 00:15:13,700
What should we do?

333
00:15:14,500 --> 00:15:15,860
I mean, Leon?

334
00:15:16,740 --> 00:15:17,540
Oh, yes

335
00:15:17,540 --> 00:15:20,020
If you three run into any trouble while you're there

336
00:15:20,020 --> 00:15:22,900
There's a special word you can say that'll probably clear it out

337
00:15:24,180 --> 00:15:24,820
Crono

338
00:15:25,540 --> 00:15:26,100
Vala

339
00:15:26,100 --> 00:15:26,660
Huh?

340
00:15:27,380 --> 00:15:28,100
You're kidding

341
00:15:28,100 --> 00:15:28,900
No way

342
00:15:29,940 --> 00:15:31,460
I can hardly believe it

343
00:15:33,300 --> 00:15:34,900
Are you friends of Crono Vala?

344
00:15:34,900 --> 00:15:39,620
That old woman was a huge help to our village

345
00:15:39,620 --> 00:15:41,700
One time when business was really slow

346
00:15:41,700 --> 00:15:44,260
She rustled off a ton of customers for me

347
00:15:44,260 --> 00:15:46,340
Man, I made a fortune that day

348
00:15:46,340 --> 00:15:48,100
But then suddenly she disappeared

349
00:15:49,460 --> 00:15:52,100
So how's that sweet little lady been doing?

350
00:15:52,100 --> 00:15:53,540
Crono Vala

351
00:15:53,540 --> 00:15:54,340
Wait

352
00:15:54,340 --> 00:15:54,820
Crono

353
00:15:55,940 --> 00:15:56,820
Nova Crono

354
00:15:57,380 --> 00:15:58,420
I get it

355
00:15:58,420 --> 00:16:01,380
When his majesty wandered out here that was the alias he used

356
00:16:02,500 --> 00:16:04,100
You guys know Crono Vala?

357
00:16:04,660 --> 00:16:05,620
Everyone loves her

358
00:16:07,060 --> 00:16:08,260
Here, take this

359
00:16:10,020 --> 00:16:13,620
All my fields were destroyed a while back so I can't offer you much

360
00:16:14,180 --> 00:16:15,860
I couldn't possibly take it for free

361
00:16:16,580 --> 00:16:17,460
Will this cover it?

362
00:16:19,860 --> 00:16:20,420
What?

363
00:16:20,420 --> 00:16:21,780
All this Yule?

364
00:16:21,780 --> 00:16:24,980
Forget the carrot, this much would buy you my whole inventory

365
00:16:24,980 --> 00:16:26,660
Go ahead and keep the rest

366
00:16:26,660 --> 00:16:28,180
Use it to help restore the village

367
00:16:28,740 --> 00:16:30,020
You sure that's okay?

368
00:16:30,580 --> 00:16:31,540
That's crazy

369
00:16:32,100 --> 00:16:33,300
I wonder who they are

370
00:16:34,100 --> 00:16:36,100
Apparently they're friends of Crono Vala's

371
00:16:36,740 --> 00:16:37,060
Hmm

372
00:16:37,700 --> 00:16:39,140
King Julius is amazing

373
00:16:39,860 --> 00:16:42,660
They respect him so deeply without even knowing it's him

374
00:16:43,220 --> 00:16:46,020
So much for not drawing attention to ourselves while we're in town

375
00:16:46,820 --> 00:16:48,420
Hopefully he's doing a better job

376
00:16:48,420 --> 00:16:52,420
Oh my goodness, do you know Crono Vala too, sir?

377
00:16:52,420 --> 00:16:55,140
That incredible woman saved my sweet baby's life

378
00:16:55,860 --> 00:16:56,660
Really?

379
00:16:56,660 --> 00:16:59,780
I went into labor while I was out in the fields one day

380
00:16:59,780 --> 00:17:01,620
And she called for a doctor to help me

381
00:17:01,620 --> 00:17:05,540
I even named him Vala after her

382
00:17:05,540 --> 00:17:07,620
Here, would you like to hold him?

383
00:17:07,620 --> 00:17:08,580
Oh no, that's alright

384
00:17:08,580 --> 00:17:15,380
I don't think I've held a baby since Noelle was this tiny

385
00:17:15,380 --> 00:17:17,220
Nose

386
00:17:17,220 --> 00:17:19,220
Nose?

387
00:17:19,220 --> 00:17:21,380
Everyone here seems to know King

388
00:17:21,380 --> 00:17:23,220
I mean Crono Vala

389
00:17:23,220 --> 00:17:25,140
Yes, I've noticed

390
00:17:26,820 --> 00:17:29,700
My name is Mayor and I'm the mayor of this village

391
00:17:29,700 --> 00:17:34,420
There isn't much that we can offer you but we'd like to invite you gentlemen to stay for the night

392
00:17:34,980 --> 00:17:37,780
Oh yeah, great idea! Stay with us!

393
00:17:37,780 --> 00:17:40,580
Our food's in short supply but we can cook for you too!

394
00:17:41,220 --> 00:17:42,420
What do you think?

395
00:17:42,420 --> 00:17:43,940
We have no reason to decline

396
00:17:44,580 --> 00:17:47,460
We were told we should mingle amongst the villagers

397
00:17:47,460 --> 00:17:49,140
And this is the perfect chance

398
00:17:50,020 --> 00:17:51,540
Well, I guess that's that then

399
00:17:56,180 --> 00:17:59,460
In the end, we didn't learn anything about the bandit attacks

400
00:18:00,180 --> 00:18:01,380
And it's not just that

401
00:18:01,940 --> 00:18:05,300
We still don't know what unfavorable activity is going on here

402
00:18:08,100 --> 00:18:09,780
What? What's happening?

403
00:18:13,700 --> 00:18:14,420
I knew it

404
00:18:16,740 --> 00:18:18,020
I think they're asleep

405
00:18:18,020 --> 00:18:18,740
Let's go

406
00:18:26,660 --> 00:18:27,780
Just as I thought

407
00:18:27,780 --> 00:18:29,940
You must be the group of bandits that we've heard about

408
00:18:30,580 --> 00:18:31,940
So what if we are?

409
00:18:31,940 --> 00:18:33,220
Give us your money now

410
00:18:33,940 --> 00:18:35,940
Unless you want to get hurt

411
00:18:35,940 --> 00:18:37,060
Take them down

412
00:18:37,780 --> 00:18:50,100
What? That can't be right

413
00:18:50,820 --> 00:18:51,540
You did this?

414
00:18:54,900 --> 00:18:57,060
I wish I could say that it came as a shock

415
00:18:57,060 --> 00:19:00,180
It's over now, everyone

416
00:19:00,180 --> 00:19:01,060
But, sir!

417
00:19:01,700 --> 00:19:02,740
We knew this would happen

418
00:19:03,460 --> 00:19:05,860
Even though we only did it so we could survive

419
00:19:06,820 --> 00:19:09,540
After the Eye of the Midnight Sun attacked

420
00:19:09,540 --> 00:19:11,460
Our village was left in shambles

421
00:19:12,340 --> 00:19:15,140
We had hoped to receive aid from the royal capital

422
00:19:15,140 --> 00:19:16,820
But no one ever came

423
00:19:16,820 --> 00:19:20,420
So we were plunged even deeper into poverty than before

424
00:19:20,420 --> 00:19:24,500
That being said, despite our intent to rebuild our village

425
00:19:24,500 --> 00:19:26,900
We were still committing a terrible crime

426
00:19:29,060 --> 00:19:31,780
I led my people to engage in this behavior

427
00:19:31,780 --> 00:19:35,140
Therefore, I ask that you allow me to take all the punishment myself

428
00:19:36,020 --> 00:19:37,540
You can't do that!

429
00:19:37,540 --> 00:19:39,220
You were only trying to help us

430
00:19:39,940 --> 00:19:42,020
I had no idea things were so dire

431
00:19:42,580 --> 00:19:45,460
If we'd been quicker to address the problem, this wouldn't have happened

432
00:19:46,500 --> 00:19:48,980
We can't let the mayor take the blame on his own

433
00:19:48,980 --> 00:19:51,380
If you're going down, we're going down with you

434
00:19:51,380 --> 00:19:52,500
No, you mustn't

435
00:20:02,020 --> 00:20:03,700
This can't possibly be real

436
00:20:04,980 --> 00:20:07,060
Lord Flegolion and Lord Nozel

437
00:20:07,060 --> 00:20:09,220
Two of the Magic Knight Captains

438
00:20:10,740 --> 00:20:13,300
You're obviously in need of our assistance

439
00:20:13,300 --> 00:20:15,140
So we can overlook what you've done

440
00:20:15,940 --> 00:20:17,940
There you go again, being too soft

441
00:20:17,940 --> 00:20:18,980
They're bandits

442
00:20:18,980 --> 00:20:21,780
They should be arrested and tried for their crimes

443
00:20:21,780 --> 00:20:24,020
Well, I'd say you're being too harsh

444
00:20:27,700 --> 00:20:32,740
I order you all to participate in the reconstruction of every village in this area

445
00:20:32,740 --> 00:20:34,420
A crime is still a crime

446
00:20:34,420 --> 00:20:36,260
And you must atone for what you've done

447
00:20:37,860 --> 00:20:39,940
So we're forgiven?

448
00:20:40,900 --> 00:20:43,700
I swear, the capital hasn't forsaken you

449
00:20:44,260 --> 00:20:47,380
But it seems that we weren't entirely aware of your situation

450
00:20:48,180 --> 00:20:52,500
We're going to make even greater strides to restore this kingdom, so please have faith in us

451
00:20:54,180 --> 00:20:55,620
Thank you so much

452
00:20:57,380 --> 00:21:00,260
That's everything we have to report from our time in Erendom

453
00:21:01,060 --> 00:21:03,700
Great job, Captains! Seems like you made the right choice

454
00:21:04,340 --> 00:21:06,580
We've sent some knights to the other villages

455
00:21:07,300 --> 00:21:10,900
That way we can determine what sort of aid each one needs and how much

456
00:21:11,940 --> 00:21:17,780
As Wizard King, my job, and yours as well, is to ensure that all of our people can live safely and peacefully

457
00:21:18,340 --> 00:21:23,300
And now that you've spent some time with them, perhaps you've learned to see their situation in a new light

458
00:21:24,340 --> 00:21:24,980
Of course

459
00:21:25,540 --> 00:21:26,900
That's why he sent us

460
00:21:26,900 --> 00:21:33,620
Captains, from now on, I want you to work even harder to lead the Magic Knights and protect this kingdom

461
00:21:33,620 --> 00:21:35,300
Yes, your majesty

462
00:21:36,740 --> 00:21:37,700
Don't let me down

463
00:21:42,740 --> 00:21:46,260
Now that that's taken care of, I think I'll wander around by myself

464
00:21:46,260 --> 00:21:47,460
Certainly not

465
00:21:47,460 --> 00:21:50,580
No? Well, then I suppose I'll check in with Yami

466
00:21:51,140 --> 00:21:54,180
I'll tell you, Marks, all this sitting around is driving me batty

467
00:21:54,180 --> 00:21:58,340
I know you feel useless

468
00:21:58,980 --> 00:22:02,020
But right now, the Clover Kingdom needs you more than you realize

469
00:22:02,020 --> 00:22:03,300
Without me

470
00:22:03,300 --> 00:22:27,500
諦めることも悪いことじゃないって あなたはいつも笑って言うけど 手を伸ばせば届くなら 紡いだ今までを 目駄にするわけにはいかない

471
00:22:27,500 --> 00:22:42,500
何度だって悔やんで 何度だって歩く そのために 突き放されるから

472
00:22:42,500 --> 00:22:56,500
正解のない旅をしよう 変わっていくことに 怖がる必要はないから

473
00:22:56,500 --> 00:23:08,500
正解のない道上 そこではきっと一人じゃない

474
00:23:08,500 --> 00:23:14,500
間違いを間違いで 終わらせないで

475
00:23:14,500 --> 00:23:20,500
涙を涙で 拭わないで

476
00:23:20,500 --> 00:23:26,500
確信がある その心を掛ける

477
00:23:26,500 --> 00:23:31,500
ここならもう一人じゃない

478
00:23:31,500 --> 00:23:49,440
次回アスターは またローマン公開けるよ

479
00:23:49,440 --> 00:23:51,440
You

